All the land that drains to one river. Rain that falls anywhere inside it ends up in the same water.

Watersheds nest. In Baltimore, rain that lands in the [[Jones Falls watershed|https://www.jonesfallswatershed.org/]] runs to the harbor, then the Patapsco, then the [[Chesapeake Bay|https://www.chesapeakebay.net/discover/watershed]].

From [[020210602000235 Ideas]]:

<<<
My house is connected to the land around it which is part of the greater watershed which is part of the bay which is part of the Atlantic which is part of Spaceship Earth… How does protecting a piedmont forest protect the bay and protect my home?
<<<

A watershed ignores county and state lines. That is why it is the usual starting point for drawing a [[BioRegion]].

It is also the root of a family of borrowed words: [[Foodshed]], [[Fibershed]], [[Plasticshed]], [[Materialshed]].

See [[Ecosystem]], [[Spaceship Earth]], [[Everything Is Connected]]

